---
title: Overview
description: What the Clients area holds, who can use it, and what each role can change.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

**Clients** holds the companies and people your firm works with: your client companies, the related companies (shareholders, billing entities, vendors), and the people behind them (directors, shareholders, contact persons). Every other part of Operon — cases, books, invoices, contracts and documents — refers to the companies kept here.

## Where it is

Select **Clients** in the left side bar. It is shown to users who have access to the CRM suite or the Secretary suite.

The panel on the left has:

| Item | Use |
|---|---|
| **Companies** | The list of companies. Opens by default. See [Companies](/en/clients/companies/). |
| **People** | The list of people. See [People](/en/clients/people/). |
| **Recently viewed** | The last five companies or people you opened, on this browser. |

## Who can change what

Most of a company's details can be changed by any user of the firm; some changes are reserved for managers.

| Action | Any user | Manager and tenant admin only |
|---|---|---|
| Create a company or a person | Yes | |
| Change a company's or a person's details | Yes | |
| Add, end or delete a relationship (director, shareholder and so on) | Yes | |
| Change the KYC conclusion | | Yes |
| Change who the company is **Assigned to** | | Yes |
| End or restore service for a client | | Yes |
| Restore deleted relationships | | Yes |
| Change who can see a company (**Access**) | Tenant admins, and people with **Can manage** on the company | |

A company can be limited to an access list; then only the people on the list can find it or open some of its information. See [Who can see a company](/en/clients/access/).

